From dc0b4238a4cfa6e1b648b2d6fb1c8c741bc89aca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FinnE145 <finne014@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:40:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] observer: no per-object proxies; reassemble Data Source;
 GetNotifications()

From a code review on 2026-10-08:

- Critical: one dasbus proxy (and D-Bus match rule) per BlueZ object,
  never released. With LE discovery (0008) bluetoothd lists dozens of
  passing devices a minute, so within ~30 min the observer hit
  dbus-daemon's 512-match-rule limit (10,163 rejections logged) and new
  subscriptions to the phone silently received nothing: "subscribed",
  zero notifications, for hours. Now bluez.py makes all calls directly on
  the connection (async, time-limited; no synchronous introspection) and
  uses a fixed set of bus-wide subscriptions dispatched by path. Tested on
  a private bus: 600 temporary devices, match rules 5 -> 5.
- Data Source responses split across several notifications are
  reassembled (long Mail bodies were cut, message_size/date lost).
- A failed GetAppAttributes no longer holds that app's notifications for
  the rest of the connection (emitted with an empty app name).
- Event facts kept per UID until removed, so repeated attribute
  responses don't lose category/flags.
- No Show after its Dismiss for notifications awaiting their app name.
- The StopNotify -> StartNotify gap (0009) is enforced per device by
  time, so overlapping subscribe attempts can't bypass it.
- Discovery control re-evaluates after every call (no scanning left on
  for a whole connection); removed devices are forgotten; a newly paired
  device's properties are read once so it subscribes without a restart.
- New GetNotifications(): per paired device the current list as
  ShowNotification JSON plus id_base / id_min / id_max.
